=== PARITY (vs web EventHistoryTable.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> NONE beyond useTranslation. The web source is a pure presentational leaf: its only hook is
    useTranslation; `history` + `isLoading` arrive as PROPS from its parent (SecurityAccessPage's security-
    history query). The native surface mirrors this — the P1/S8 EventHistorySource carries that parent prop
    snapshot (events / isLoading / an optional error); the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> EventHistoryProjection.resolve is the native port of the web render ladder
    `isLoading ? <Skeleton lines={8}/> : <DataTable data=history emptyMessage=… />`: loading wins (web checks
    isLoading first), then the native error branch, then rows.isEmpty ? empty : data. The helpers.ts logic is
    ported 1:1 in EventHistoryAdapter and exercised end-to-end by executed XCTest:
      • parseWindowState: closed/"0"->Closed, contains "vent"->Venting, any other non-empty->Open.
      • doorClosed: null->true; bool-> !state; number-> ==0; object-> every member false/null; string->
        trimmed sentinels (""/closed/closedall/0/false), `{`-prefixed JSON whose members are all false/null,
        else open.
      • allWindowsClosed / windowSummary (All Closed | N Open/Venting) over fd/fp/rd/rp.
      • Lock/Sentry use JS truthiness exactly as the web `row.locked ?` / `row.sentryMode ?` (a non-empty
        string such as "off" is truthy — preserved, with a regression test pinning it).
  Composition -> FadeIn(delay 0.3) -> GlassPanel(p-4) -> <h2>Security Event History</h2> (isHeader trait) ->
    body switch. Columns reproduce the web eventColumns: Time (TimeStamp, sortable) · Lock (Badge
    success/danger Locked/Unlocked) · Sentry (Badge success/neutral On/Off) · Doors (green/amber text,
    asNonEmptyString(doorState) ?? Closed/—) · Windows (green/amber text, windowSummary). Rendered through the
    shared TSDataTable (web DataTable, compact).
  Shared components -> @/components/ui -> shared TSDataTable (web DataTable), TSGlassPanel (web GlassPanel),
    runtime status badge mirroring TSBadge tokens (web Badge — taking the facade-resolved string the
    LocalizedStringKey-only TSBadge can't express); @/components/feedback -> TSSkeleton (web Skeleton);
    @/components/motion -> TSFadeIn (web FadeIn). Compiled against the REAL apps/apple component library in the
    iOS+macOS typechecks below. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> loading (8-line skeleton) · data (table) · empty (web DataTable emptyMessage —
    "No security events recorded yet.") · error (native QueryError-equivalent + retry).
    NOTE on stale/offline (the generic P4 states list): the web leaf has NO stale/offline chrome — it is
    presentational (only hook useTranslation; no query/connectivity at this level), and its parent owns the
    security-history query. An upstream/connectivity failure is surfaced through the native `error` snapshot
    (with a retry affordance, the QueryError-equivalent the states contract asks for). Inventing separate
    stale/offline chrome here would be drift from the spec ("web source is THE specification"); it is
    deliberately not added — identical disposition to the 0009 presentational-leaf predecessor. Each state has
    a #if DEBUG preview and is unit-tested via the projection.
  i18n -> all 12 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    admin.security.eventHistory, .col.time, .col.lock, .locked, .unlocked, .col.sentry, .on, .off, .col.doors,
    .closed, .col.windows, .noEvents — ALL present in EventHistoryTable.strings, plus the two windowSummary
    phrases (helpers.ts hardcodes "All Closed" / "{n} Open/Venting"; routed through the facade here so native
    code holds no literals) and 3 native chrome/a11y keys (loading / error title / retry). No English literals
    in native code (Text(verbatim:) over the facade).
  a11y -> the <h2> carries the header trait; the retry button has an accessibilityLabel; the loading state is
    one labeled element; the empty/error states are combined elements; Doors/Windows/Time cells carry value
    labels; EventHistoryAccessibility.rowSummary is a tested combined-value seam (Time/Lock/Sentry/Doors/
